WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:02.756
(dramatic music)

00:00:02.756 --> 00:00:03.700
(crowd shouts in foreign language)

00:00:03.700 --> 00:00:05.220
(protester shouts in foreign language)

00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:08.340
- [Dov] From blocking highways
to forming human chains

00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:09.720
and dressing up as characters

00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:11.707
from Margaret Atwood's dystopian novel,

00:00:11.707 --> 00:00:12.993
"The Handmaid's Tale."

00:00:12.993 --> 00:00:14.130
(protesters singing in foreign language)

00:00:14.130 --> 00:00:16.440
- [Dov] For three months, up
to half a million Israelis

00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:18.270
have taken to the streets
across the country

00:00:18.270 --> 00:00:20.130
to protest a judicial overhaul planned

00:00:20.130 --> 00:00:22.380
by Prime Minister Benjamin
Netanyahu's government.

00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:24.840
The growing revolt piled
pressure on Netanyahu

00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:27.240
to suspend the overhaul
until parliament reconvenes

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:28.820
at the end of April.

00:00:28.820 --> 00:00:33.320
(Benjamin speaks in foreign language)

00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:38.850
- Here's what happening in Israel,

00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:41.280
the stakes behind Netanyahu's
judicial overhaul,

00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:43.262
and where things could be headed next.

00:00:43.262 --> 00:00:45.360
(tense music)

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:46.350
There are many layers to it,

00:00:46.350 --> 00:00:48.330
but there are three things
you need to understand.

00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:51.630
First is changing the
committee that appoints judges.

00:00:51.630 --> 00:00:55.470
This overhaul will give the
ruling coalition a majority

00:00:55.470 --> 00:00:58.080
on that committee and that will allow them

00:00:58.080 --> 00:01:01.230
to place like-minded judges on the bench.

00:01:01.230 --> 00:01:03.480
The second pillar of the judicial overhaul

00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:05.400
is to limit the jurisdiction of the court.

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:08.700
That means what cases will
the court be able to hear?

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:11.940
And the third thing, and perhaps
the most controversial bit,

00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:13.620
is what's called the Override Clause.

00:01:13.620 --> 00:01:16.710
That will allow a simple
majority of parliament,

00:01:16.710 --> 00:01:19.470
meaning 61 of 120 lawmakers,

00:01:19.470 --> 00:01:22.320
to override decisions
of the Supreme Court.

00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:24.180
Netanyahu and his collation partners

00:01:24.180 --> 00:01:26.190
say this judicial overhaul is necessary

00:01:26.190 --> 00:01:28.020
in order to balance out the court.

00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:30.450
They say that the court
is dominated by liberals

00:01:30.450 --> 00:01:31.950
and that it's way too activist,

00:01:31.950 --> 00:01:34.470
the court itself needs
a check on its power

00:01:34.470 --> 00:01:38.370
because it is a essentially
blocking the will of the people.

00:01:38.370 --> 00:01:40.110
For people who oppose the overhaul,

00:01:40.110 --> 00:01:42.510
they believe it will undermine
the Supreme Court completely.

00:01:42.510 --> 00:01:45.330
- Well, we came here to
protest against the degradation

00:01:45.330 --> 00:01:47.700
of the Israeli democracy.

00:01:47.700 --> 00:01:51.360
We see a process where
the rights of the people

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:56.360
will be overtime consumed by
this theocratic government.

00:01:56.520 --> 00:01:58.290
- These protests have really exposed

00:01:58.290 --> 00:02:00.720
long-held divisions in Israeli society

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:02.790
between its secular side

00:02:02.790 --> 00:02:05.035
and its religious, more conservative side.

00:02:05.035 --> 00:02:06.570
(tense music continues)

00:02:06.570 --> 00:02:09.570
One of the major problems of this overhaul

00:02:09.570 --> 00:02:12.270
for the protesters is
that it's being advanced

00:02:12.270 --> 00:02:14.190
by Prime Minister Netanyahu himself.

00:02:14.190 --> 00:02:17.100
Netanyahu has long been
a defender of the Court

00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:19.440
and they ask themselves, "Why is Netanyahu

00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:22.350
suddenly supporting this
massive judicial overhaul?"

00:02:22.350 --> 00:02:24.210
And for them, the answer is clear.

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:27.990
It's because Benjamin Netanyahu
is on trial for corruption,

00:02:27.990 --> 00:02:30.900
and if this overhaul passes
they believe he will use it

00:02:30.900 --> 00:02:33.720
in order to get out of
his own legal problems.

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:35.430
Netanyahu denies this,

00:02:35.430 --> 00:02:38.633
but the protesters at this
point simply do not believe him.

00:02:38.633 --> 00:02:40.564
(protesters singing in foreign language)

00:02:40.564 --> 00:02:41.397
(whistle blaring)
(protesters shouting)

00:02:41.397 --> 00:02:43.920
- After Netanyahu has paused legislation,

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:47.100
it will be very, very
difficult for the opposition

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:49.920
and ruling coalition to find
an agreement on this issue

00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:52.590
because they are so
far apart as it stands.

00:02:52.590 --> 00:02:55.110
Perhaps the opposition and the coalition

00:02:55.110 --> 00:02:56.370
will find a compromise,

00:02:56.370 --> 00:02:59.790
but if they don't we can expect
this conflict to come back

00:02:59.790 --> 00:03:01.192
and to come back stronger.

00:03:01.192 --> 00:03:05.371
(machinery whirs)
(intense music)

